Four NAK code generation changes from Mesa main that are in no Mesa release yet. Upstream text (MIT licence),
unchanged, oldest first:
  commit 5e4bcb1c nak,nvk: Increase nir_opt_peephole limit
  commit b6b973d0 nak: Fix ready_cycle calculation in prepass sched
  commit a79e3fc7 nak: Move FutureReadyInstr::new into postpass.rs
  commit cb0e7868 nak: Always apply opt_fall_through
None is specific to one GPU generation and none fixes wrong output: they change the code generated for every shader.
Peephole limit: NIR turns an if into selects when its sides hold up to 8 cheap ALU instructions (was: moves only), for
every stage; the chain already did that for compute shaders.
Ready cycle: the scheduler that orders instructions before register allocation took every instruction's ready cycle
as 0 (it read a field this pass never updates), so latencies played no part in the order; it now uses the value it
tracks. The dependency graph is unchanged: the new order is another legal order of the same graph. The commit after
it moves the old helper to the only pass that still uses it.
Fall-through: a branch to the next block is removed also when jump threading changed nothing.
This is the patch to leave out first when a rendering fault has to be narrowed down:
NVK_SKIP_PATCHES=nvk-nak-sched-main for build/build_nvk.sh.

